<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>A credential value originating from <code>KyotoUAuth</code> is returned
from a <code>__repr__</code> or <code>__str__</code> method. These
methods are invoked implicitly any time the object is printed, formatted
into an f-string, displayed in a debugger, or dumped as part of frame
locals in a stack trace. A password embedded in their return value is
trivially exposed.</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>Render only non-sensitive identifying information from
<code>__repr__</code> / <code>__str__</code>. The <code>username</code>
and class name are typically enough.</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Bad:</p>
<sample language="python">
class KyotoUAuth:
    def __repr__(self) -> str:
        return f"KyotoUAuth(user={self._username}, pw={self._password})"
</sample>

<p>Good:</p>
<sample language="python">
class KyotoUAuth:
    def __repr__(self) -> str:
        return f"KyotoUAuth(user={self._username})"
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>CWE-200: Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor
(<a href="https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html">cwe.mitre.org/200</a>).</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
